  "description": "Local times at daylight-saving and other offset changes, and the UTC instant native TaskJuggler 3.8.4 gives each one (TjTime parses a date with Ruby's Time.local, which on glibc searches with localtime_r). 'local' is TaskJuggler date text read in 'zone' as the project time zone; 'utc' is the instant. Checked natively by `node engine/golden/tz-edges.mjs --native` (and before every golden recording) and in the wasm engine by `node engine/golden/tz-edges.mjs` and `npm run golden:wasm`. Kinds: gap (the local time does not exist), overlap (it happens twice), before and after (the last and first unambiguous times around a change), plain (no change nearby).",
